{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Current Gap\n\nStories 1934, 749c, 1fd4, and 0b14 landed authenticated `undeclared`, `paths`, and `none` behavior. Current-state inspection of `docs/plan-review-gate.md` shows no explicit section enumerating those three states and no author-facing explanation of `set-file-impact --none`. This ticket CREATES that missing documentation; the acceptance criteria below describe the required end state, not current behavior.\n\nThis story edits repository files, so its own scope is `paths`, never `none`.\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n1. Create an explicit tri-state section in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`. Define each state and freshness effect; state the live-child neutral/poison roll-up; state declaration changes affect the material fingerprint; include a mixed paths-plus-none example.\n2. Update `docs/ticket-model.md` beside file impact with the same three persisted states. State docs-only and test-only work touches repository files and therefore declares paths.\n3. Reconcile `docs/event-schema.md` FILE_IMPACT wording with the landed event keys and transition semantics.\n4. Update `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, the packaged source for public `rebar explain plan`. Explain when `set-file-impact --none` is truthful, when it is not, and how `no-file-impact` LLM review judges the reason. A substantive reason identifies why the work produces no repository-file change and where its output/evidence lives; vague claims such as docs-only are invalid because docs are repository files.\n5. RED-first, add `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract` to `tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py`. Invoke the public CLI entry point with `main([\"explain\", \"plan\"])`, capture stdout, and assert the rendered author contract exposes: the three choices `undeclared`, `paths`, and `none`; the command `set-file-impact --none`; the boundary that none means no repository file; docs-only/test-only use paths; LLM review; and the substantive-reason rule. The test must not open or grep the guide source, inspect registry internals, or assert formatting/section order. Run the exact node before prose changes and require RED because the public output lacks this guidance; run it after prose changes and require GREEN.\n6. Run `pytest -q tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py::test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract`, `make lint`, and the full test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A new `docs/plan-review-gate.md` tri-state section explicitly defines `undeclared` as conservative whole-HEAD fallback.\n- [ ] The same section defines `paths` as dependency-scoped freshness.\n- [ ] The same section defines `none` as an authenticated declaration that contributes no file dependencies.\n- [ ] The gate doc states live `none` children are neutral.\n- [ ] The gate doc states live undeclared children poison inheritance and closed children are ignored.\n- [ ] The gate doc states declaration changes alter the material fingerprint.\n- [ ] The gate doc includes a worked mixed-scope example where a paths child contributes dependencies and a none child does not.\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` documents all three states beside file impact.\n- [ ] `docs/ticket-model.md` states docs-only and test-only work declares paths, not none.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` documents `file_impact`, `file_impact_scope`, and `no_file_impact_reason` plus clearing semantics.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output exposes the three choices and `set-file-impact --none`.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output states none means no repository file is touched.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output states docs-only/test-only work uses paths.\n- [ ] Public `rebar explain plan` output states the none claim is LLM-reviewed and a substantive reason must explain both why no repository file changes and where output/evidence lives.\n- [ ] `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract` passes through the public CLI output and contains no source-file reads, source grep, private-shape assertion, or formatting-order assertion.\n- [ ] No production logic or schema file changes; under `src/rebar`, only `_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md` changes.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] The full test suite passes."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785262372005210001,"uuid":"ccf93ed0-f29c-4a10-9b47-f07117a6dc5e"}